    funnelStage: "bofu", ctaType: B, conceptBucket: "proven", effort: "high",
    bodyBlack: "Most founders raise prices reactively, when costs go up. Here's the framework I use to decide proactively instead.\nSignal 1: your close rate on new deals is above 70% for 2 consecutive months -- that's a clear sign you're priced under the market's actual ceiling.\nSignal 2: you've delivered a specific, measurable improvement to your process since your last price -- price should track value delivered, not only time passed.\nSignal 3: your best clients would still say yes at 15-20% more, based on what they've told you the work is worth to them.\nAny two of these three, and it's time -- not \"eventually,\" the next new client.\nComment \"RAISE\" and I'll DM you the exact script I use to introduce a new, higher price to a new prospect.",
