    pillar: "authority", contentType: "educational", angle: "Educational Tip / Hack", format: "Voiceover Format",
    funnelStage: "mofu", ctaType: M, conceptBucket: "proven", effort: "high",
    bodyBlack: "If a prospect is comparing you on price, that's not a pricing problem -- it's a positioning problem that happened earlier in the funnel.\nWhen your messaging describes the same category as every competitor, price becomes the only remaining differentiator left for the buyer to judge you on.\nThe fix isn't a discount. It's naming a specific, narrower category you're the obvious best fit for, so there's nothing directly comparable to price-check against.\nI've watched founders \"win\" a price war and still lose the account, because winning on price trains that client to always shop on price with you.\nComment \"POSITION\" and I'll send you the exact repositioning exercise I run with clients stuck comparing on price.",
    bodyRed: "No on-camera talking -- voiceover over relevant b-roll (two near-identical price tags).", bodyGreen: "On-screen text: \"positioning problem, not a pricing problem\".",
    ctaLine: "Comment POSITION and I'll send you the exact repositioning exercise.",
