    funnelStage: "bofu", ctaType: B, conceptBucket: "proven", effort: "high",
    bodyBlack: "If a founder hired me with a roadmap twice as long as their team could realistically ship, here's exactly how I'd cut it in half.\nDay 1: score every item against the core metric it's supposed to move -- if it doesn't clearly move it, it's out immediately.\nDays 2-4: for everything that survives, ask if a smaller version could validate the same assumption in a quarter of the time.\nDays 5-7: rank what's left by impact-to-effort, and cut the roadmap at the exact point where the team's real capacity ends -- not where ambition wants it to end.\nDay 8: communicate the cuts explicitly, with the reasoning, not silently -- teams trust a roadmap more when they understand what got cut and why.\nComment \"ROADMAP2\" and I'll DM you the scoring template we use for the cut.",
